/ One meeting that discussed the Drucksache, with what its minutes record:
/ meeting and decision above, the text below. Longer minutes start as an
/ excerpt whose toggle swaps it for the full text, very long ones link to the
/ minutes instead of putting all of it on the page.
- text = Parsing.text(item.minutes).to_s
- minutes_path = minutes_meeting_path(item.meeting, anchor: item.id)
.py-2.border-top
  .small.text-secondary.mb-1
    => l item.meeting.date
    ' ·
    => link_to item.meeting.committee&.name || item.meeting.title, meeting_path(item.meeting), class: 'link-secondary'
    ' ·
    => link_to "TOP #{item.number}", minutes_path, class: 'link-secondary'
    = meeting_result_badge(item)
  - if text.length <= 600
    .allris-content
      == meeting_format(item.minutes, item.meeting)
  - else
    .collapse.show id="discussion-#{item.id}-excerpt" class="discussion-#{item.id}"
      p.mb-0
        => truncate(text, length: 400, separator: ' ')
        - if text.length > 5000
          = link_to 'Im Protokoll weiterlesen', minutes_path
        - else
          button.btn.btn-link.p-0.align-baseline type='button' data-bs-toggle='collapse' data-bs-target=".discussion-#{item.id}" aria-expanded='false' aria-controls="discussion-#{item.id}-full"
            | weiterlesen
    - if text.length <= 5000
      .collapse.allris-content id="discussion-#{item.id}-full" class="discussion-#{item.id}"
        == meeting_format(item.minutes, item.meeting)
